cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A proof of the Regts–Sevenster conjecture, formalized: a Lean 4
  development
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite both the software and
  the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: William
    family-names: Whistler
    email: will@whistler.uk
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-03"
url: https://github.com/WillWhistler/Regts-Sevenster
repository-code: https://github.com/WillWhistler/Regts-Sevenster
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of both directions of the Regts–Sevenster
  conjecture: a complex-valued graph parameter normalized at the
  empty graph has exponentially bounded edge-connection rank if and
  only if it is a mixed partition function, with the model's numbers
  of even and odd colours bounded by ⌊2eR⌋. Both directions are
  proved outright, and so is the fibre-functor form of Deligne's
  theorem on tensor categories,
  on which the forward direction rests. The development carries no
  sorry, no custom axiom and no native_decide, and pins the axiom set
  of every main theorem to [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - graph parameter
  - connection matrix
  - mixed partition function
  - edge-colouring model
  - symmetric tensor category
  - super vector space
  - fibre functor
references:
